# Shell scripts run on Linux servers no matter which OS committed them, and a
# CRLF line ending breaks the shebang outright — `env: bash\r: No such file or
# directory` — rather than failing at any point that says why. Forced to LF
# regardless of a contributor's own core.autocrlf, so a script that works on
# the machine that wrote it also works on the machine that runs it.
*.sh text eol=lf
deploy/b-ui text eol=lf
